{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `R`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added `R_safestan_copy`, a deterministic copy of `R`, because the original model uses `R` in transformed data and parameter bounds before the observation statement. Replaced the manual Jacobian/prior contribution `target += -2 * log(N)` with the built-in prior statement `N ~ pareto(C - R_safestan_copy + M, 1)`, whose log density is proportional to `-2 * log(N)` on the same support. The binomial observation of `R` is unchanged and remains the protected likelihood term.

Deterministic data augmentation: `R_safestan_copy = R`; for the supplied data this is `0`.
","model_safe_stan":"/*
 * mark-recpapture-2 prior:
 *
 *   theta ~ uniform(0, M / (C - R + M))
 * 
 * reparameterized in temrs of N:
 *
 *   (M / N) ~ uniform(0, M / (C - R + M));
 * 
 * requires Jacobian adjustment:
 *
 *   function:      f(N) -> M / N
 *   derivative:    f'(N)  =  -M / N^2
 *   Jacobian adj:  abs(f'(N)) = M / N^2
 *   log Jac adj:   log(abs(f'(N)) = log(M) - 2 * log(N)
 *   drop const:    -2 * log(N)
 */

data {
  int<lower=0> M;
  int<lower=0> C;
  int<lower=0, upper=min(M, C)> R;
  int<lower=0, upper=min(M, C)> R_safestan_copy;
}
transformed data {
  real theta_max;
  theta_max = M;
  theta_max = theta_max / (C - R_safestan_copy + M);
}
parameters {
  real<lower=(C - R_safestan_copy + M)> N;
}
transformed parameters {
  real<lower=0, upper=theta_max> theta;
  theta = M / N;
}
model {
  N ~ pareto(C - R_safestan_copy + M, 1);
  R ~ binomial(C, theta);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"C":3,"M":3,"R":0,"R_safestan_copy":0}","protected_variables":["R"]}
